        "exact_choice_count": null,
        "notes": "Scheduled intakes July each year. Application processing Please refer to the Certificate in Essential Technical Skills for Architecture, Construction, and Engineering for application processing dates. Recommended for success To be successful in this program, students are recommended to possess the following: English language proficiency: Category 3 \u2013 English Studies 12 (50%) or equivalent High school completion (or equivalent) Good computer proficiency, including Microsoft Word and Microsoft Excel Good communication skills and/or the desire to develop good communication skills An interest in exploring careers in the fields of architecture, construction, construction management, or engineering Access to a personal computer at home International applicants This program is not available to international students. View available programs . Apply to program There is no requirement to apply to this microcredential. If you are interested, you may apply for the Certificate in Essential Technical Skills for Architecture, Construction, and Engineering . The first three courses of that program comprise this microcredential. Please contact Ann Martineau for more information. Go back Overview Next up Costs & Supplies",
